  "interpretation": "The same two current narrow checkers inspect all retained drafts offline. Original scores, outcomes, source excerpts and human-review statuses are unchanged. These are known development examples, not a new model run or quality estimate.",
  "implementation": [
    "Draft-only known positive first-person tracker mutation patterns require a bounded correction.",
    "Known positive closure-to-fix links, closed/resolved pairs and resolved/handled-in-tracker wording require correction.",
    "Aggregate both kinds in one feedback message; retain the existing evidence checkpoint, request caps, feedback reserve and rejection audit.",
    "Known negations, modal suggestions, questions and local attribution remain allowed. Source excerpts are never rewritten.",
    "Both evaluation paths use the same helpers and leave missing final content unscored."
